      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "In a recent study in Nature Medicine, Rauber et al. (2017) identify interleukin-9 (IL-9) derived from group 2 innate lymphoid cells as crucial regulators inducing resolution of chronic inflammation in rheumatoid arthritis. Their findings provide insight into the varied functions of IL-9 and open the door to novel therapeutic interventions."
